        "content_hash": "54df73a64761179b5018c231b315d6c614282f026639493f0cc6d971c0cbc055"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For probability laws pi,mu, every measurable incidence E of product mass alpha>0, and every finite-valued query-dependent map T_f, put beta(f)=mu(E_f), S={beta>0}, and K_f=(mu x mu){T_f(v)=T_f(v')}. If integral_S K_f dpi<=K, then H(T_F(V)|F;(pi x mu)|E)>=-log K+2 log alpha. The density coefficient 2 is optimal without additional hypotheses.",
