    {
      "claim_id": "CP_WEIGHTED_OVERLAPS",
      "version": 2,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_CP",
        "content_hash": "54df73a64761179b5018c231b315d6c614282f026639493f0cc6d971c0cbc055"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Under the matched equal-slope spatial rate realizations of proj:tied, every dense parameter restriction yields a dense set of full-spatial overlaps of exponent L=p+H+g. Rich inputs have dense weight for one original conditional Frostman (p+g) planar law and scalar projections w_f+(r_d-r_f)(t_d-t_f)x with support exponent at most g. The coefficient theorem and the weighted projection test then imply g>=f_s(p), while monotonicity and the off-tie scalar bound imply H>=f_s(p).",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "593a349c6775a6ca46dc3e5d7a1013659da1d8b93a1db6560630c617ad9f1269"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CP_QUANTITATIVE",
      "version": 3,
      "context": {
